module

import all Init.Data.Repr
public import CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.VIR.VectorReduce
public import CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.VIR.JasminDialect
public import CatCrypt.Crypto.Pairing.MsmReduce
public import CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.Dialects.OrchestrationFront

/-!
# Production BLS12-381 emit: G1/G2 group leaves, the pairing leaf, the MSM
  reduction over the production G1 group, and the verifier equations

`MsmReduce.lean` validated the **MSM = `scalarFold` over the EC group** reduction
on a *toy* curve (`ZMod 23`), with the EC point-add / scalar-mul as opaque
`extCall` leaves (`MsmReduce.EcLeafAgrees`). This file is its **production
analogue at BLS12-381**: the same `VectorReduce.scalarFold_eq_hsum` core, over
the production G1 additive group, the same opaque-leaf edge, plus the
**pairing** (Miller loop + final exponentiation) as a *separate* opaque leaf —
the piece `MsmReduce`'s docstring flagged as out of scope there. With the pairing
leaf in hand we emit the three pairing-equation **verifiers** (Groth16, KZG, BLS)
as straight-line `Com` compositions of the pairing / EC leaves.

## No new machinery — the AUCurves-leaf story

The positioning is exactly the FAEST symmetric-leaf / AUCurves-leaf pattern: the
field/group/pairing primitives are **leaves** (no new VIR machinery), and the
front emits them as opaque `extCall`s whose *agreement* (`EcLeafAgrees`,
`PairingLeafAgrees`) ties the opaque leaf to the abstract primitive. The
production witness is the AUCurves verified-bedrock2 BLS12-381 tower
(AUCurves, `bls12_381_safe.rs`: `fp_*`, `fp2_*`, `fp12_*`,
`miller_loop`, `pairing`), which CatCrypt already rust-cmd-links in
`bench/kzg/src/aucurves_backend.rs` (the verified piece there is precisely
`miller_loop` + `final_exp` + `fp12_mul` + `fp_opp`). G1/G2 group add/scalar-mul
are leaves AUCurves exposes at the group level via `blst` in that backend; the
agreement here is the same opaque edge.

* the **MSM reduction** (`msmFold_eq_msm`) is `MsmReduce.msm_eq_scalarFold` at the
  production G1 `AddCommMonoid` lane — no new content;
* the **verifier equations** are straight-line compositions of leaves, each with
  a denotation-preservation theorem reducing the `Com` to the abstract primitives.
  Each such theorem takes the leaf model as a parameter `leafSem`, denotes the
  `Com` through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem`, and assumes the agreements at that
  `leafSem`; `Bls12381Denote.bls12381Oracle` satisfies them for every `prims`.

## The production G1 group (the AddCommMonoid lane)

Like `VectorReduce` (which is generic over *any* `AddCommMonoid`), the MSM
reduction needs only that the BLS12-381 G1 group is an `AddCommMonoid`
(associativity + commutativity let the accumulation reassociate / reorder). We
therefore take the production group as an abstract `[AddCommMonoid G1]`: the
concrete G1 is the BLS12-381 r-torsion subgroup of
`E(Fp)` (an abelian group), but we do not re-derive a 381-bit primality `decide`
to obtain Mathlib's affine-point `AddCommGroup` (infeasible for a 381-bit prime).
The reduction is sound for the production group *because* it is an
`AddCommMonoid`, which is exactly the carried hypothesis. The toy
`MsmReduce.ECPt` over `ZMod 23` is the concrete `AddCommMonoid` instance that
*validates* the same reduction at a field where the EC ops are schoolbook.

## Wire layout (production widths)

A BLS12-381 base-field element `Fp` is 6 little-endian `u64` limbs = `48` bytes
(`FPSZ`). On the wire:
* a **G1 point** is `(x ‖ y)`, two `Fp`s = `2·FPSZ = 96` bytes;
* a **G2 point** is `(x ‖ y)` over `Fp2 = Fp × Fp`, four `Fp`s = `4·FPSZ = 192`
  bytes;
* the pairing output **GT = Fp12** is twelve `Fp`s = `12·FPSZ = 576` bytes.
These match the AUCurves `Fp([u64;6])` / `Fp2` / `Fp12` layouts exactly.

## KAT / bench

* `bench/bls12381_compare/` — G1 add + scalar-mul + pairing KAT against the
  AUCurves verified reference, anchored to the **published standard BLS12-381
  generators** `G1`, `G2` (the KAT-vector Montgomery limbs in
  `bls12-381-safe-rust/tests/kat_vectors.rs` decode byte-identically to the
  published `G1.x = 0x17f1d3a7…b22c6bb` from RFC 9380 §8.8.1 /
  draft-irtf-cfrg-pairing-friendly-curves) and the precomputed GT generator
  `e(G1,G2)`.
* `bench/groth16_compare/`, `bench/kzg_compare/` — the verifier-equation KATs: a
  self-consistent prove-then-verify pair generated by the AUCurves reference,
  whose EC/pairing leaf values match the published curve generators.

All goals closed; the only hypotheses are the opaque-leaf agreements
(`EcLeafAgrees` / `PairingLeavesAgree`) at the leaf-model parameter `leafSem`.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace CatCrypt.Crypto.Pairing.Bls12381Emit

open CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.VIR
open CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.VIR.JasminDialect
open CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.VIR.VectorReduce
open CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.Dialects.OrchestrationFront
open scoped BigOperators

/-! ## 1. Production wire widths -/

/-- A BLS12-381 base-field element `Fp` on the wire: `48` bytes (6 little-endian
    `u64` limbs), matching the AUCurves `Fp([u64;6])` layout. -/
def FPSZ : Nat := 48

/-- A G1 point on the wire: `(x ‖ y)`, two `Fp`s = `96` bytes. -/
def G1SZ : Nat := 2 * FPSZ

/-- A G2 point on the wire: `(x ‖ y)` over `Fp2 = Fp × Fp`, four `Fp`s = `192`
    bytes. -/
def G2SZ : Nat := 4 * FPSZ

/-- A GT element `Fp12` on the wire: twelve `Fp`s = `576` bytes (the pairing /
    Miller-loop output). -/
def GTSZ : Nat := 12 * FPSZ

/-! ## 2. The MSM reduction over the production G1 group (the main result)

The MSM `Σ_i k_i · P_i` over the BLS12-381 G1 group. As in `VectorReduce`, the
only algebraic fact the reduction needs is that the lane type is an
`AddCommMonoid`; we take the production G1 group as an abstract `[AddCommMonoid
G1]` (the BLS12-381 r-torsion subgroup is an abelian group). This is
`MsmReduce.msm_eq_scalarFold` re-stated at the production lane. -/

section MSM

variable {G1 : Type*} [AddCommMonoid G1] {L : ℕ}

/-- The MSM as the **horizontal reduction** `hsum` over the production G1 group of
    the per-term scalar-multiples `k_i • P_i` — the value `Σ_i k_i · P_i` a packed
    scalar-mul + tree point-add computes. -/
def msm (k : Fin L → ℕ) (P : Fin L → G1) : G1 :=
  hsum (fun i => (k i) • (P i))

/-- The MSM as the **sequential left-fold** `scalarFold` the straight-line emitter
    produces: `((0 + k₀·P₀) + k₁·P₁) + ⋯`, G1 point-adds threaded left to right. -/
def msmFold (k : Fin L → ℕ) (P : Fin L → G1) : G1 :=
  scalarFold (fun i => (k i) • (P i))

/-- **The main result (production lane).** The BLS12-381 MSM reduces to
    `scalarFold` over the production G1 `AddCommMonoid`: the sequential left-fold
    (what the straight-line / loop emitter produces) equals the horizontal
    reduction (what a packed scalar-mul + tree point-add computes). This is
    `VectorReduce.scalarFold_eq_hsum` instantiated at the production G1 lane — no
    new content; the G1 group's `AddCommMonoid` laws are exactly what let the
    accumulation reassociate / reorder. -/
theorem msmFold_eq_msm (k : Fin L → ℕ) (P : Fin L → G1) :
    msmFold k P = msm k P :=
  scalarFold_eq_hsum (fun i => (k i) • (P i))

/-- The BLS12-381 MSM computes the mathematical multi-scalar multiplication
    `Σ_i k_i · P_i` (the commitment Groth16 / KZG / Bulletproofs realize over the
    SRS / powers-of-τ). -/
theorem msm_isSum (k : Fin L → ℕ) (P : Fin L → G1) :
    msm k P = ∑ i, (k i) • (P i) := by
  simp only [msm, hsum]

end MSM

/-! ## 3. The EC + pairing leaf spec (opaque `extCall`, carried agreement)

The G1/G2 point-add and scalar-mul are the **EC leaf** (`MsmReduce.EcLeafAgrees`
shape, at production widths). The Miller-loop + final-exp **pairing** is a
*separate* opaque leaf (`PairingLeafAgrees`). Both are declared in the exact
`MsmReduce` named-leaf shape: a named-leaf semantics carrier
(reusing `MsmReduce.EcLeafSem`), the abstract primitives, and the agreement
tying the opaque leaf to those primitives. The leaves are *opaque*; their
agreements are the carried obligation, never an admitted proof. -/

/-- The leaf name the front emits for G1 point-add. -/
def g1AddLeafName : String := "g1_add"

/-- The leaf name the front emits for G1 scalar-multiply. -/
def g1MulLeafName : String := "g1_scalar_mul"

/-- The leaf name the front emits for G2 point-add. -/
def g2AddLeafName : String := "g2_add"

/-- The leaf name the front emits for G2 scalar-multiply. -/
def g2MulLeafName : String := "g2_scalar_mul"

/-- The leaf name the front emits for the BLS12-381 pairing (Miller loop + final
    exponentiation), `e : G1 × G2 → GT`. The AUCurves verified witness is
    `bls12_pairing(out, p_x, p_y, q_x, q_y)`. -/
def pairingLeafName : String := "bls12_pairing"

/-- The leaf name the front emits for the GT (`Fp12`) multiply — the
    pairing-product accumulator op (AUCurves `bls12_Fp12_mul`). -/
def fp12MulLeafName : String := "fp12_mul"

/-! ### Dialect signatures (production widths) -/

/-- G1 point-add leaf signature: `(P, Q : stackArr 8 G1SZ) → R : stackArr 8 G1SZ`. -/
def g1AddArgTys : List JasminTy := [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ]
/-- G1 scalar-mul leaf signature: `(k : stackArr 8 FPSZ, P : stackArr 8 G1SZ) → R`. -/
def g1MulArgTys : List JasminTy := [.stackArr 8 FPSZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ]
/-- Both G1 leaves return a G1 point. -/
def g1RetTy : JasminTy := .stackArr 8 G1SZ

/-- G2 point-add leaf signature: `(P, Q : stackArr 8 G2SZ) → R : stackArr 8 G2SZ`. -/
def g2AddArgTys : List JasminTy := [.stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]
/-- G2 scalar-mul leaf signature: `(k : stackArr 8 FPSZ, P : stackArr 8 G2SZ) → R`. -/
def g2MulArgTys : List JasminTy := [.stackArr 8 FPSZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]
/-- Both G2 leaves return a G2 point. -/
def g2RetTy : JasminTy := .stackArr 8 G2SZ

/-- Pairing leaf signature: `(P : stackArr 8 G1SZ, Q : stackArr 8 G2SZ) → GT`. -/
def pairingArgTys : List JasminTy := [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]
/-- The pairing leaf returns a GT (`Fp12`) element. -/
def gtRetTy : JasminTy := .stackArr 8 GTSZ

/-- GT-multiply leaf signature: `(a, b : stackArr 8 GTSZ) → stackArr 8 GTSZ`. -/
def fp12MulArgTys : List JasminTy := [.stackArr 8 GTSZ, .stackArr 8 GTSZ]

/-- The leaf-semantics carrier (reusing `MsmReduce.EcLeafSem`: the exact shape of
    `jasminExtSem`). A concrete binding (the AUCurves-backed leaves) is a value
    of this type. -/
abbrev LeafSem : Type := MsmReduce.EcLeafSem

/-- The abstract BLS12-381 primitive interface the emit orchestrates: G1/G2
    point-add + scalar-multiply, the pairing `e`, and the GT product, on the
    on-wire byte representations. -/
structure BlsPrimitives where
  /-- G1 point addition `P + Q`. -/
  g1Add : (Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8)
  /-- G1 scalar multiplication `k · P`. -/
  g1Mul : (Fin FPSZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8)
  /-- G2 point addition `P + Q`. -/
  g2Add : (Fin G2SZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin G2SZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin G2SZ → BitVec 8)
  /-- G2 scalar multiplication `k · P`. -/
  g2Mul : (Fin FPSZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin G2SZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin G2SZ → BitVec 8)
  /-- The BLS12-381 pairing `e(P, Q) : GT` (Miller loop + final exponentiation). -/
  pairing : (Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin G2SZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin GTSZ → BitVec 8)
  /-- The GT (`Fp12`) product `a · b`. -/
  fp12Mul : (Fin GTSZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin GTSZ → BitVec 8) → (Fin GTSZ → BitVec 8)

/-! ### Per-leaf agreements (opaque leaf realises the abstract primitive) -/

/-- G1 point-add leaf agreement. -/
def G1AddLeafAgrees (prims : BlsPrimitives) (leafSem : LeafSem) : Prop :=
  ∀ args : HVector (fun t => ⟦t⟧) g1AddArgTys,
    leafSem g1AddLeafName g1AddArgTys g1RetTy args = prims.g1Add (args.head) (args.tail.head)

/-- G1 scalar-mul leaf agreement. -/
def G1MulLeafAgrees (prims : BlsPrimitives) (leafSem : LeafSem) : Prop :=
  ∀ args : HVector (fun t => ⟦t⟧) g1MulArgTys,
    leafSem g1MulLeafName g1MulArgTys g1RetTy args = prims.g1Mul (args.head) (args.tail.head)

/-- G2 point-add leaf agreement. -/
def G2AddLeafAgrees (prims : BlsPrimitives) (leafSem : LeafSem) : Prop :=
  ∀ args : HVector (fun t => ⟦t⟧) g2AddArgTys,
    leafSem g2AddLeafName g2AddArgTys g2RetTy args = prims.g2Add (args.head) (args.tail.head)

/-- G2 scalar-mul leaf agreement. -/
def G2MulLeafAgrees (prims : BlsPrimitives) (leafSem : LeafSem) : Prop :=
  ∀ args : HVector (fun t => ⟦t⟧) g2MulArgTys,
    leafSem g2MulLeafName g2MulArgTys g2RetTy args = prims.g2Mul (args.head) (args.tail.head)

/-- **Pairing leaf agreement.** On the `bls12_pairing` signature, the leaf
    semantics is `prims.pairing` of its G1 + G2 arguments — the opaque-leaf edge
    for the Miller loop + final exponentiation. The AUCurves verified
    `bls12_pairing` is the intended witness. -/
def PairingLeafAgrees (prims : BlsPrimitives) (leafSem : LeafSem) : Prop :=
  ∀ args : HVector (fun t => ⟦t⟧) pairingArgTys,
    leafSem pairingLeafName pairingArgTys gtRetTy args
      = prims.pairing (args.head) (args.tail.head)

/-- GT-multiply leaf agreement (the pairing-product accumulator). -/
def Fp12MulLeafAgrees (prims : BlsPrimitives) (leafSem : LeafSem) : Prop :=
  ∀ args : HVector (fun t => ⟦t⟧) fp12MulArgTys,
    leafSem fp12MulLeafName fp12MulArgTys gtRetTy args
      = prims.fp12Mul (args.head) (args.tail.head)

/-- The full EC-leaf agreement (`MsmReduce.EcLeafAgrees` analogue, production
    widths): the leaf realises G1 + G2 point-add and scalar-mul. The validated
    AUCurves group leaves are the intended witness (`bench/bls12381_compare/`). -/
def EcLeafAgrees (prims : BlsPrimitives) (leafSem : LeafSem) : Prop :=
  G1AddLeafAgrees prims leafSem ∧ G1MulLeafAgrees prims leafSem ∧
    G2AddLeafAgrees prims leafSem ∧ G2MulLeafAgrees prims leafSem

/-- The full pairing-side agreement: the pairing leaf and the GT-multiply leaf
    both agree with the abstract primitives. The AUCurves `bls12_pairing` +
    `bls12_Fp12_mul` are the intended witnesses. -/
def PairingLeavesAgree (prims : BlsPrimitives) (leafSem : LeafSem) : Prop :=
  PairingLeafAgrees prims leafSem ∧ Fp12MulLeafAgrees prims leafSem

/-! ## 4. Leaf `Expr` builders + denotation (the `extCall` bridge point)

Mirror of `MsmReduce.{ecAddLeafExpr, ecMulLeafExpr}` and their `*_denote`
theorems, at the production leaves. Denoted through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem`,
each leaf `Expr` is (by `rfl`) `leafSem` of the looked-up arguments, which a leaf
agreement at `leafSem` rewrites to the abstract primitive. -/

/-- Build the G1 point-add leaf `Expr` from two G1-point variables. -/
def g1AddLeafExpr {Γ : Ctxt jasminDialect} (P Q : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 G1SZ)) :
    Expr jasminDialect Γ g1RetTy :=
  { op := .extCall g1AddLeafName g1AddArgTys g1RetTy, retTy_eq := rfl,
    args := .cons P (.cons Q .nil) }

/-- Build the G1 scalar-mul leaf `Expr` from a scalar variable and a G1 point. -/
def g1MulLeafExpr {Γ : Ctxt jasminDialect}
    (k : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 FPSZ)) (P : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 G1SZ)) :
    Expr jasminDialect Γ g1RetTy :=
  { op := .extCall g1MulLeafName g1MulArgTys g1RetTy, retTy_eq := rfl,
    args := .cons k (.cons P .nil) }

/-- Build the BLS12-381 pairing leaf `Expr` from a G1 point and a G2 point. -/
def pairingLeafExpr {Γ : Ctxt jasminDialect}
    (P : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 G1SZ)) (Q : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 G2SZ)) :
    Expr jasminDialect Γ gtRetTy :=
  { op := .extCall pairingLeafName pairingArgTys gtRetTy, retTy_eq := rfl,
    args := .cons P (.cons Q .nil) }

/-- Build the GT-multiply leaf `Expr` from two GT (`Fp12`) variables. -/
def fp12MulLeafExpr {Γ : Ctxt jasminDialect}
    (a b : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 GTSZ)) :
    Expr jasminDialect Γ gtRetTy :=
  { op := .extCall fp12MulLeafName fp12MulArgTys gtRetTy, retTy_eq := rfl,
    args := .cons a (.cons b .nil) }

/-- Denoted through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem`, the G1 point-add leaf `Expr` is
    `leafSem` of the looked-up points. By `rfl`. -/
theorem g1AddLeafExpr_denote (leafSem : LeafSem) {Γ : Ctxt jasminDialect}
    (P Q : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 G1SZ)) (V : Ctxt.Valuation Γ) :
    @Expr.denote _ _ _ (jasminDenoteWith leafSem) _ _ (g1AddLeafExpr P Q) V
      = leafSem g1AddLeafName g1AddArgTys g1RetTy
          (.cons (P.lookup V) (.cons (Q.lookup V) .nil)) :=
  rfl

/-- Denoted through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem`, the G1 scalar-mul leaf `Expr` is
    `leafSem` of the looked-up scalar and point. By `rfl`. -/
theorem g1MulLeafExpr_denote (leafSem : LeafSem) {Γ : Ctxt jasminDialect}
    (k : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 FPSZ)) (P : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 G1SZ))
    (V : Ctxt.Valuation Γ) :
    @Expr.denote _ _ _ (jasminDenoteWith leafSem) _ _ (g1MulLeafExpr k P) V
      = leafSem g1MulLeafName g1MulArgTys g1RetTy
          (.cons (k.lookup V) (.cons (P.lookup V) .nil)) :=
  rfl

/-- Denoted through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem`, the pairing leaf `Expr` is
    `leafSem` of the looked-up G1 and G2 points. By `rfl`; `PairingLeafAgrees`
    at `leafSem` rewrites it to `prims.pairing`. -/
theorem pairingLeafExpr_denote (leafSem : LeafSem) {Γ : Ctxt jasminDialect}
    (P : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 G1SZ)) (Q : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 G2SZ))
    (V : Ctxt.Valuation Γ) :
    @Expr.denote _ _ _ (jasminDenoteWith leafSem) _ _ (pairingLeafExpr P Q) V
      = leafSem pairingLeafName pairingArgTys gtRetTy
          (.cons (P.lookup V) (.cons (Q.lookup V) .nil)) :=
  rfl

/-- Denoted through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem`, the GT-multiply leaf `Expr` is
    `leafSem` of the looked-up GT operands. By `rfl`. -/
theorem fp12MulLeafExpr_denote (leafSem : LeafSem) {Γ : Ctxt jasminDialect}
    (a b : Ctxt.Var Γ (.stackArr 8 GTSZ)) (V : Ctxt.Valuation Γ) :
    @Expr.denote _ _ _ (jasminDenoteWith leafSem) _ _ (fp12MulLeafExpr a b) V
      = leafSem fp12MulLeafName fp12MulArgTys gtRetTy
          (.cons (a.lookup V) (.cons (b.lookup V) .nil)) :=
  rfl

/-! ## 5. One MSM term over G1, with the denotation carry

Production analogue of `MsmReduce.msmTermCom` / `msmTermCom_denote`: one MSM step
`acc ↦ acc + k_i · P_i` over the G1 group, built from the two G1 leaves, denoting
to `prims.g1Add acc (prims.g1Mul k P)` through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem` for every
leaf oracle `leafSem` satisfying `EcLeafAgrees`. The full
straight-line MSM is this step folded `L` times, matched at the G1 lane by
`msmFold_eq_msm`. -/

/-- One G1 MSM step as an orchestrating `Com` over `(acc, k, P)` — the
    **hand-authored shadow**, the proven-equal reference for the front-sourced
    deployed `g1MsmTermCom`: first the G1 scalar-mul leaf `t = g1_scalar_mul(k, P)`,
    then the G1 point-add leaf `out = g1_add(acc, t)`. This is the `scalarFold`
    body `acc ↦ acc + k_i·P_i`. -/
def g1MsmTermComShadow :
    Com jasminDialect
      [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 FPSZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ]
      (.stackArr 8 G1SZ) :=
  -- Γ = [acc, k, P]
  .var (g1MulLeafExpr
          (Γ := [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 FPSZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ])
          (.there .here) (.there (.there .here)))
    -- Γ' = [t, acc, k, P]
    (.var (g1AddLeafExpr
            (Γ := [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ,
                   .stackArr 8 FPSZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ])
            (.there .here) .here)
      (.ret .here))

/-- The G1 MSM step as an `OrchestrationFront` phase schedule: `t =
    g1_scalar_mul(k, P)` (operand slots `[1, 0]`), `out = g1_add(acc, t)` (slots
    `[2, 3]`). Root slots on `[acc, k, P]`: `acc = 2, k = 1, P = 0`; the call
    results `t, out` take slots `3, 4`. -/
def g1MsmTermSchedule : List CallPhase :=
  [ { leaf := g1MulLeafName, argTys := g1MulArgTys, retTy := g1RetTy,
      argSlots := [1, 0] }        -- t = g1_scalar_mul(k, P)
  , { leaf := g1AddLeafName, argTys := g1AddArgTys, retTy := g1RetTy,
      argSlots := [2, 3] } ]      -- out = g1_add(acc, t)

/-- **Generation gate.** The front resolves the G1 MSM-step schedule. -/
theorem g1MsmTermCom_isSome :
    (buildOrchCom [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 FPSZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ]
      g1MsmTermSchedule 4 (.stackArr 8 G1SZ)).isSome = true := by rfl

/-- **The deployed G1 MSM step, front-sourced.** Generated by
    `OrchestrationFront.buildOrchCom` from `g1MsmTermSchedule` — the front SOURCES
    this orchestration (it is not hand-authored). Definitionally equal to the hand
    shadow (`g1MsmTermCom_eq_shadow`), so it lowers to the same owned-x86 `.s`. -/
def g1MsmTermCom :
    Com jasminDialect
      [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 FPSZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ]
      (.stackArr 8 G1SZ) :=
  (buildOrchCom [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 FPSZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ]
    g1MsmTermSchedule 4 (.stackArr 8 G1SZ)).get g1MsmTermCom_isSome

/-- **Exactness.** The front-sourced deployed `g1MsmTermCom` is *definitionally*
    the hand shadow — the auto-resolved de-Bruijn operand chains coincide with the
    hand-threaded `.here`/`.there` chains, so every downstream fact transfers. -/
theorem g1MsmTermCom_eq_shadow : g1MsmTermCom = g1MsmTermComShadow := by rfl

/-- **The deployed G1 MSM step, evaluated with a leaf oracle.** For a leaf oracle
    `leafSem` realising the EC group primitives (`EcLeafAgrees prims leafSem`), the
    deployed `g1MsmTermCom`, denoted through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem`, computes
    `prims.g1Add acc (prims.g1Mul k P)`, the `scalarFold` body `acc + k·P`. The
    leaf model is the parameter `leafSem`; `Bls12381Denote` instantiates it. -/
theorem g1MsmTermCom_denote (leafSem : LeafSem) (prims : BlsPrimitives)
    (hLeaf : EcLeafAgrees prims leafSem)
    (acc : Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8) (k : Fin FPSZ → BitVec 8) (P : Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8) :
    @Com.denote _ _ _ (jasminDenoteWith leafSem) _ _
        g1MsmTermCom (.cons acc (.cons k (.cons P .nil)))
      = prims.g1Add acc (prims.g1Mul k P) := by
  rw [g1MsmTermCom_eq_shadow]
  obtain ⟨hAdd, hMul, _, _⟩ := hLeaf
  show leafSem g1AddLeafName g1AddArgTys g1RetTy
        (.cons acc (.cons (leafSem g1MulLeafName g1MulArgTys g1RetTy
                            (.cons k (.cons P .nil))) .nil))
      = prims.g1Add acc (prims.g1Mul k P)
  rw [hMul (.cons k (.cons P .nil))]
  simp only [HVector.head, HVector.tail]
  rw [hAdd (.cons acc (.cons (prims.g1Mul k P) .nil))]
  rfl

/-! ## 6. The verifier equations (straight-line `Com` compositions of leaves)

Each pairing-equation verifier is a straight-line `Com` of pairing + GT-multiply
leaves; its denotation through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem` reduces (under
`PairingLeavesAgree prims leafSem`) to the
abstract product of pairings. The check itself (`= 1` in GT) is the caller's
final equality test on the denoted value.

Convention: each verifier denotes to the **left-hand-side pairing product** the
verifier accumulates. The verification equation holds iff this product equals
the right-hand side (or, in the negate-and-multiply form used by
`aucurves_backend.rs`, iff `final_exp` of the combined product is `1`). -/

/-! ### 6a. BLS signature verify: `e(σ, G2) = e(H(m), pk)`

Two pairings: `e(σ, G2)` (signature × generator) and `e(H(m), pk)` (hashed
message × public key). The verifier computes both and compares. We emit the
straight-line `Com` computing the pair `(e(σ,G2), e(H(m),pk))` packed; here we
expose the *left* pairing `e(σ, G2)` and prove its denotation. -/

/-- BLS verify, left pairing `e(σ, G2)` — the **hand-authored shadow**: a single
    pairing leaf over `(σ, G2)`. `Γ = [σ : G1, G2 : G2]`. -/
def blsVerifyLhsComShadow :
    Com jasminDialect [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ] (.stackArr 8 GTSZ) :=
  .var (pairingLeafExpr
          (Γ := [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]) .here (.there .here))
    (.ret .here)

/-- The single-pairing verifier-LHS phase schedule (shared by BLS-verify LHS
    `e(σ, G2)` and KZG-opening LHS `e(π, [s−z]G2)` — the identical single-pairing
    orchestration): one `pairing` leaf over slots `[1, 0]`. Root slots on
    `[P : G1, Q : G2]`: `P = 1, Q = 0`; the result takes slot `2`. -/
def singlePairingLhsSchedule : List CallPhase :=
  [ { leaf := pairingLeafName, argTys := pairingArgTys, retTy := gtRetTy,
      argSlots := [1, 0] } ]      -- out = pairing(P, Q)

/-- **Generation gate.** The front resolves the single-pairing LHS schedule. -/
theorem blsVerifyLhsCom_isSome :
    (buildOrchCom [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]
      singlePairingLhsSchedule 2 (.stackArr 8 GTSZ)).isSome = true := by rfl

/-- **The deployed BLS-verify LHS, front-sourced** by `buildOrchCom` from
    `singlePairingLhsSchedule`. Definitionally the hand shadow
    (`blsVerifyLhsCom_eq_shadow`). -/
def blsVerifyLhsCom :
    Com jasminDialect [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ] (.stackArr 8 GTSZ) :=
  (buildOrchCom [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]
    singlePairingLhsSchedule 2 (.stackArr 8 GTSZ)).get blsVerifyLhsCom_isSome

/-- **Exactness.** The front-sourced deployed `blsVerifyLhsCom` is *definitionally*
    the hand shadow. -/
theorem blsVerifyLhsCom_eq_shadow : blsVerifyLhsCom = blsVerifyLhsComShadow := by rfl

/-- **The deployed BLS-verify LHS, evaluated with a leaf oracle.** For a leaf
    oracle `leafSem` realising the pairing primitives
    (`PairingLeavesAgree prims leafSem`), the deployed `blsVerifyLhsCom`, denoted
    through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem`, computes `prims.pairing σ G2`. The full
    check `e(σ,G2) = e(H(m),pk)` is the caller comparing this to the RHS pairing. -/
theorem blsVerifyLhsCom_denote (leafSem : LeafSem) (prims : BlsPrimitives)
    (hPair : PairingLeavesAgree prims leafSem)
    (sig : Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8) (g2 : Fin G2SZ → BitVec 8) :
    @Com.denote _ _ _ (jasminDenoteWith leafSem) _ _
        blsVerifyLhsCom (.cons sig (.cons g2 .nil))
      = prims.pairing sig g2 := by
  rw [blsVerifyLhsCom_eq_shadow]
  obtain ⟨hP, _⟩ := hPair
  show leafSem pairingLeafName pairingArgTys gtRetTy
        (.cons sig (.cons g2 .nil)) = prims.pairing sig g2
  rw [hP (.cons sig (.cons g2 .nil))]
  rfl

/-! ### 6b. KZG opening verify: `e(π, [s−z]G2) = e(C − [y]G1, G2)`

Two pairings over precomputed G1/G2 inputs: the quotient-commitment pairing
`e(π, [s−z]G2)` (LHS) and `e(C−[y]G1, G2)` (RHS). We expose the LHS pairing and
prove its denotation; the verifier compares it to the RHS pairing. -/

/-- KZG opening verify, LHS pairing `e(π, [s−z]G2)` — the **hand-authored
    shadow**: one pairing leaf over `(π, sMinusZ_G2)`. `Γ = [π : G1, [s−z]G2 : G2]`.
    -/
def kzgVerifyLhsComShadow :
    Com jasminDialect [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ] (.stackArr 8 GTSZ) :=
  .var (pairingLeafExpr
          (Γ := [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]) .here (.there .here))
    (.ret .here)

/-- **Generation gate.** The front resolves the single-pairing LHS schedule (shared
    with BLS-verify LHS — the identical single-pairing orchestration). -/
theorem kzgVerifyLhsCom_isSome :
    (buildOrchCom [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]
      singlePairingLhsSchedule 2 (.stackArr 8 GTSZ)).isSome = true := by rfl

/-- **The deployed KZG-verify LHS, front-sourced** by `buildOrchCom` from the
    shared `singlePairingLhsSchedule`. Definitionally the hand shadow
    (`kzgVerifyLhsCom_eq_shadow`). -/
def kzgVerifyLhsCom :
    Com jasminDialect [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ] (.stackArr 8 GTSZ) :=
  (buildOrchCom [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]
    singlePairingLhsSchedule 2 (.stackArr 8 GTSZ)).get kzgVerifyLhsCom_isSome

/-- **Exactness.** The front-sourced deployed `kzgVerifyLhsCom` is *definitionally*
    the hand shadow. -/
theorem kzgVerifyLhsCom_eq_shadow : kzgVerifyLhsCom = kzgVerifyLhsComShadow := by rfl

/-- **The deployed KZG-verify LHS, evaluated with a leaf oracle.** For a leaf
    oracle `leafSem` realising the pairing primitives
    (`PairingLeavesAgree prims leafSem`), the deployed `kzgVerifyLhsCom`, denoted
    through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem`, computes `prims.pairing π ([s−z]G2)`. The
    full check is the caller comparing this to the RHS pairing `e(C−[y]G1, G2)`. -/
theorem kzgVerifyLhsCom_denote (leafSem : LeafSem) (prims : BlsPrimitives)
    (hPair : PairingLeavesAgree prims leafSem)
    (proof : Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8) (sMinusZ_g2 : Fin G2SZ → BitVec 8) :
    @Com.denote _ _ _ (jasminDenoteWith leafSem) _ _
        kzgVerifyLhsCom (.cons proof (.cons sMinusZ_g2 .nil))
      = prims.pairing proof sMinusZ_g2 := by
  rw [kzgVerifyLhsCom_eq_shadow]
  obtain ⟨hP, _⟩ := hPair
  show leafSem pairingLeafName pairingArgTys gtRetTy
        (.cons proof (.cons sMinusZ_g2 .nil)) = prims.pairing proof sMinusZ_g2
  rw [hP (.cons proof (.cons sMinusZ_g2 .nil))]
  rfl

/-! ### 6c. Groth16 verify: `e(A,B) = e(αG1,βG2) · e(L,γG2) · e(C,δG2)`

The pairing-product equation. The RHS is the product of three pairings; we emit
the straight-line `Com` accumulating that product via two GT-multiplies, and
prove its denotation is `prims.fp12Mul (prims.fp12Mul e1 e2) e3` where
`e1 = e(αG1,βG2)`, `e2 = e(L,γG2)`, `e3 = e(C,δG2)`. The verifier checks this
equals `e(A,B)`. -/

/-- Groth16 verify, RHS pairing-product
    `e(αG1,βG2) · e(L,γG2) · e(C,δG2)` — the **hand-authored shadow**. Three pairing
    leaves followed by two GT-multiplies, left-associated. ABI:
    `Γ = [αG1, βG2, L, γG2, C, δG2]` (G1, G2, G1, G2, G1, G2). -/
def groth16VerifyRhsComShadow :
    Com jasminDialect
      [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ,
       .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]
      (.stackArr 8 GTSZ) :=
  -- Γ0 = [αG1, βG2, L, γG2, C, δG2]
  .var (pairingLeafExpr
          (Γ := [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ,
                 .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ])
          .here (.there .here))  -- e1 = e(αG1, βG2)
    -- Γ1 = [e1, αG1, βG2, L, γG2, C, δG2]
    (.var (pairingLeafExpr
            (Γ := [.stackArr 8 GTSZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ,
                   .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ,
                   .stackArr 8 G2SZ])
            (.there (.there (.there .here)))            -- L
            (.there (.there (.there (.there .here)))))  -- γG2
      -- Γ2 = [e2, e1, αG1, βG2, L, γG2, C, δG2]
      (.var (pairingLeafExpr
              (Γ := [.stackArr 8 GTSZ, .stackArr 8 GTSZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ,
                     .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ,
                     .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ])
              (.there (.there (.there (.there (.there (.there .here))))))            -- C
              (.there (.there (.there (.there (.there (.there (.there .here)))))))) -- δG2
        -- Γ3 = [e3, e2, e1, ...]
        (.var (fp12MulLeafExpr
                (Γ := [.stackArr 8 GTSZ, .stackArr 8 GTSZ, .stackArr 8 GTSZ,
                       .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ,
                       .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ])
                (.there (.there .here)) (.there .here))  -- e1 · e2
          -- Γ4 = [p12, e3, e2, e1, ...]
          (.var (fp12MulLeafExpr
                  (Γ := [.stackArr 8 GTSZ, .stackArr 8 GTSZ, .stackArr 8 GTSZ,
                         .stackArr 8 GTSZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ,
                         .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ,
                         .stackArr 8 G2SZ])
                  .here (.there .here))  -- (e1·e2) · e3
            (.ret .here)))))

/-- The Groth16 RHS pairing-product as an `OrchestrationFront` phase schedule.
    Root slots on `[αG1, βG2, L, γG2, C, δG2]`: `αG1 = 5, βG2 = 4, L = 3, γG2 = 2,
    C = 1, δG2 = 0`. Three `pairing` leaves — `e1 = e(αG1,βG2)` (slots `[5,4]` →
    slot `6`), `e2 = e(L,γG2)` (`[3,2]` → `7`), `e3 = e(C,δG2)` (`[1,0]` → `8`) —
    then two `fp12_mul` leaves — `p12 = e1·e2` (`[6,7]` → `9`), `out = p12·e3`
    (`[9,8]` → `10`, returned). -/
def groth16VerifyRhsSchedule : List CallPhase :=
  [ { leaf := pairingLeafName, argTys := pairingArgTys, retTy := gtRetTy,
      argSlots := [5, 4] }        -- e1 = e(αG1, βG2)
  , { leaf := pairingLeafName, argTys := pairingArgTys, retTy := gtRetTy,
      argSlots := [3, 2] }        -- e2 = e(L, γG2)
  , { leaf := pairingLeafName, argTys := pairingArgTys, retTy := gtRetTy,
      argSlots := [1, 0] }        -- e3 = e(C, δG2)
  , { leaf := fp12MulLeafName, argTys := fp12MulArgTys, retTy := gtRetTy,
      argSlots := [6, 7] }        -- p12 = e1 · e2
  , { leaf := fp12MulLeafName, argTys := fp12MulArgTys, retTy := gtRetTy,
      argSlots := [9, 8] } ]      -- out = p12 · e3

/-- **Generation gate.** The front resolves the Groth16 RHS schedule. -/
theorem groth16VerifyRhsCom_isSome :
    (buildOrchCom
      [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ,
       .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]
      groth16VerifyRhsSchedule 10 (.stackArr 8 GTSZ)).isSome = true := by rfl

/-- **The deployed Groth16 RHS pairing-product, front-sourced** by `buildOrchCom`
    from `groth16VerifyRhsSchedule`. Definitionally the hand shadow
    (`groth16VerifyRhsCom_eq_shadow`). -/
def groth16VerifyRhsCom :
    Com jasminDialect
      [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ,
       .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]
      (.stackArr 8 GTSZ) :=
  (buildOrchCom
    [.stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ,
     .stackArr 8 G2SZ, .stackArr 8 G1SZ, .stackArr 8 G2SZ]
    groth16VerifyRhsSchedule 10 (.stackArr 8 GTSZ)).get groth16VerifyRhsCom_isSome

/-- **Exactness.** The front-sourced deployed `groth16VerifyRhsCom` is
    *definitionally* the hand shadow. -/
theorem groth16VerifyRhsCom_eq_shadow :
    groth16VerifyRhsCom = groth16VerifyRhsComShadow := by rfl

/-- **The deployed Groth16 verifier RHS product, evaluated with a leaf oracle.**
    For a leaf oracle `leafSem` realising the pairing primitives
    (`PairingLeavesAgree prims leafSem`), the deployed `groth16VerifyRhsCom`,
    denoted through `jasminDenoteWith leafSem`, computes the left-associated
    product of three pairings
    `prims.fp12Mul (prims.fp12Mul (e αG1 βG2) (e L γG2)) (e C δG2)`. The verifier
    checks this equals `e(A, B)`. -/
theorem groth16VerifyRhsCom_denote (leafSem : LeafSem) (prims : BlsPrimitives)
    (hPair : PairingLeavesAgree prims leafSem)
    (aG1 : Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8) (bG2 : Fin G2SZ → BitVec 8)
    (l : Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8) (gG2 : Fin G2SZ → BitVec 8)
    (c : Fin G1SZ → BitVec 8) (dG2 : Fin G2SZ → BitVec 8) :
    @Com.denote _ _ _ (jasminDenoteWith leafSem) _ _
        groth16VerifyRhsCom
        (.cons aG1 (.cons bG2 (.cons l (.cons gG2 (.cons c (.cons dG2 .nil))))))
      = prims.fp12Mul
          (prims.fp12Mul (prims.pairing aG1 bG2) (prims.pairing l gG2))
          (prims.pairing c dG2) := by
  rw [groth16VerifyRhsCom_eq_shadow]
  obtain ⟨hP, hM⟩ := hPair
  show leafSem fp12MulLeafName fp12MulArgTys gtRetTy
        (.cons (leafSem fp12MulLeafName fp12MulArgTys gtRetTy
                  (.cons (leafSem pairingLeafName pairingArgTys gtRetTy
                            (.cons aG1 (.cons bG2 .nil)))
                    (.cons (leafSem pairingLeafName pairingArgTys gtRetTy
                              (.cons l (.cons gG2 .nil))) .nil)))
          (.cons (leafSem pairingLeafName pairingArgTys gtRetTy
                    (.cons c (.cons dG2 .nil))) .nil))
      = prims.fp12Mul
          (prims.fp12Mul (prims.pairing aG1 bG2) (prims.pairing l gG2))
          (prims.pairing c dG2)
  rw [hP (.cons aG1 (.cons bG2 .nil)), hP (.cons l (.cons gG2 .nil)),
      hP (.cons c (.cons dG2 .nil))]
  simp only [HVector.head, HVector.tail]
  rw [hM (.cons (prims.pairing aG1 bG2) (.cons (prims.pairing l gG2) .nil))]
  simp only [HVector.head, HVector.tail]
  rw [hM (.cons (prims.fp12Mul (prims.pairing aG1 bG2) (prims.pairing l gG2))
            (.cons (prims.pairing c dG2) .nil))]
  rfl

end CatCrypt.Crypto.Pairing.Bls12381Emit
